                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Aion was clearly a good MMO at some point in the past, but today the game is so bad that it is not even worth launching. I wanted to play it to prepare for Aion 2 because I wanted to be familiar with the lore and get my first experience with the franchise. Unfortunately, the experience was really, really bad in almost every aspect.\r\n\r\nLevel Design - 2.5/5: It's pretty mid. The environments are interesting, but the game barely makes use of its verticality. You can only fly in very restricted areas, and I never even got the chance to engage in aerial combat, which is a shame.\r\n\r\nWorld Design - 1.5/5: Really bad. There are very few maps, and while doing some research and watching videos about the lore, I learned that there used to be many more maps, with coherent progression and much richer lore. Clearly, that is no longer the case here. You spend 65 levels in a single map doing pointless repeatable quests. It's a shame because the other maps I got to explore are really beautiful and could provide an excellent setting for a good story.\r\n\r\nMain Character - 0.5/5: I followed absolutely every dialogue, and I still have no idea what the MC's role is. I know the character was changed following updates, but in the current version, the MC is just awful. Clearly lazy writing.\r\n\r\nVillain - 0.5/5: Apparently, there used to be a main villain for each expansion, but that is no longer the case. The story is told in such a terrible way that it is difficult to understand who the main antagonist is, what their motivations are, and so on. During one questline, an antagonist was mentioned, only for them to disappear. Then, in another questline, I learned that they had been defeated, with absolutely no context. Clearly a terrible experience.\r\n\r\nCast - 0.5/5: I have never seen so many bland characters. None of them has any personality, they come and go without warning, the dialogue is awful... What a disaster. The MC is supposed to have a best friend who has been accompanying them since the beginning, and this is the worst-written friendship I have ever seen. There is clearly no effort behind any of this. An AI could have written the dialogue.\r\n\r\nStory - 0.5/5: Just as terrible as the cast and the villain. The story is completely disjointed, it is told in an awful way, events follow one another without anything making sense... What an unpleasant experience. The worst part is that I watched a two-hour video about Aion's lore after my playthrough, and it was genuinely interesting. The lore seemed rich, the storylines were intriguing, and the foundations were incredibly solid. But apparently, they decided to remove content (for reasons nobody knows) and piece together whatever was left without caring whether the result would be coherent or understandable. Even after thinking about it, I still cannot understand what led to such decisions. Why would you want to kill a game that the developers must have spent an enormous amount of time building? What a disappointment.\r\n\r\nEnding - 0.5/5: I don't even want to spend time talking about it. Since the story makes no sense, neither does the ending, obviously.\r\n\r\nGameplay - 2.5/5: There are some good things here. I played Sorceress and enjoyed the class. Clearly, every class has its own unique traits and its own role within a group. The problem is that the game is dead, so there is no group content to speak of. As for the quests, you are always doing the same things, so there is no reason to expect any depth. What a shame.\r\n\r\nSound Experience - 4.5/5: The game's real strength. The music is simply excellent.\r\n\r\nArt Direction - 3.5/5: The art direction is coherent, and even though the whole \"angels vs. demons\" concept is not particularly original, it is handled relatively well. There are some genuinely great ideas, but since the game's content has been drastically reduced, we can only appreciate them on a small scale.\r\n\r\nThe average across my categories is 1.7/5. The game is clearly bad, and I am surprised it is still available. It is nothing more than a shell of what it once was, and this clearly doesn't bode well for Aion 2, which already has very aggressive monetization. I hope it won't suffer the same fate as its older brother, but I am not very optimistic.\r\n\r\nTotal playtime : 15h19\r\nGrade : 3/10",
